<title>JAPAN: Tokyo precious metals market closed on Thursday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo precious metals market closed on Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo precious metals market is closed on Thursday for the Sports Day holiday and will reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, TOCOM's most-active August 1997 gold settled four yen higher at 1,349 yen per gram, while other precious metals were narrowly mixed.</p>
